CAT = "zare5Framework"; SEG = "FWK"
Q = [
("What is the main purpose of the FAIS Act?",
 "To regulate advice and intermediary services", ["To set the capital rules that insurers follow", "To regulate credit agreements with consumers", "To control foreign exchange transactions"],
 "The Financial Advisory and Intermediary Services Act 37 of 2002 regulates the rendering of financial advice and intermediary services to clients. Insurer solvency falls under the Insurance Act and credit agreements under the National Credit Act."),
("Which body administers the FAIS Act today?",
 "The FSCA", ["The Prudential Authority", "The National Credit Regulator", "The Financial Intelligence Centre"],
 "Since the Financial Sector Regulation Act took effect in 2018, the FSCA, which replaced the Financial Services Board, administers the FAIS Act. The Prudential Authority supervises the safety and soundness of financial institutions."),
("Under the FAIS Act, a 'financial service' means:",
 "Advice or an intermediary service", ["Only the sale of an insurance policy", "Any service a bank provides", "Advice given only for a fee"],
 "The Act defines financial service as any service contemplated in the definitions of advice and intermediary service. Whether a fee is charged does not decide it."),
("Which of these is a financial product under the FAIS Act?",
 "A unit trust investment", ["A vehicle finance agreement", "A personal loan from a bank", "A clothing store account"],
 "A participatory interest in a collective investment scheme (a unit trust) is a financial product. Credit agreements such as loans and vehicle finance are regulated by the National Credit Act, not FAIS."),
("A client puts money in a fixed deposit at a bank. Under the FAIS Act, the deposit is:",
 "A financial product", ["A credit agreement under the NCA", "Outside FAIS because banks are exempt", "A product only if held for five years"],
 "A deposit as defined in the Banks Act is listed as a financial product in the FAIS Act, so advice on it is a financial service."),
("A broker helps a client choose a medical scheme option. The broker is:",
 "Rendering a financial service", ["Outside the FAIS Act entirely", "Acting only under the Banks Act", "Giving only factual information"],
 "Health service benefits provided by a medical scheme are financial products under FAIS. A medical scheme broker also needs accreditation from the Council for Medical Schemes."),
("Which of these is advice under the FAIS Act?",
 "Recommending a specific policy", ["Explaining how to fill in a claim form", "Describing a product's features objectively", "Giving the insurer's contact details"],
 "Advice is a recommendation, guidance or proposal of a financial nature about buying, investing in or changing a financial product. Procedural help and objective descriptions are excluded."),
("A representative tells a client, without recommending anything, which form to complete to switch funds. This is:",
 "Not advice under the FAIS Act", ["Advice, because it concerns a product", "Advice only if given by telephone", "Advice if the client then switches"],
 "Factual information given merely on the procedure for entering into a transaction is excluded from the definition of advice."),
("Which of these is an intermediary service?",
 "Submitting a client's claim", ["Recommending a retirement annuity", "Analysing a client's financial needs", "Proposing a change of investment fund"],
 "An intermediary service is an act other than advice, done for a client or product supplier, that leads to a transaction or involves administering the product, such as receiving, submitting or processing claims. The other three are advice or part of it."),
("Collecting premiums from clients on behalf of a product supplier is:",
 "An intermediary service", ["Advice under the FAIS Act", "A clerical act outside FAIS", "A service no FSP may render"],
 "Collecting or accounting for premiums or other money payable by a client to a product supplier is named in the definition of intermediary service."),
("Under the FAIS Act, a product supplier is the person who:",
 "Issues a financial product", ["Sells products on behalf of an FSP", "Approves the FSP's licence", "Supervises the representatives"],
 "A product supplier issues a financial product, for example an insurer or a collective investment scheme manager. Intermediaries sell or administer the product for clients or suppliers."),
("Under the FAIS Act, the term 'client' includes:",
 "A third party acting for the client", ["Only individuals, never companies", "Only people who have bought a product", "Only people who pay a fee"],
 "A client is a specific person or group of persons, including a third party acting on their behalf, to whom a financial service is rendered. Companies can be clients too."),
("Which of these is a long-term policy as defined in the Long-term Insurance Act?",
 "A funeral policy", ["A household contents policy", "A motor vehicle policy", "A medical scheme option"],
 "Long-term policies include assistance (such as funeral), disability, fund, health, life and sinking fund policies. Contents and motor cover are short-term insurance; a medical scheme option is a health service benefit."),
("A policy that pays a client's legal liability for damage they cause to other people's property is:",
 "A short-term insurance policy", ["A long-term insurance policy", "A health service benefit", "A collective investment scheme"],
 "Liability cover is a short-term (non-life) insurance policy. Long-term policies pay on events such as death or disability."),
("A benefit that a pension fund provides to its members because of their membership is:",
 "A financial product under FAIS", ["Excluded because it is compulsory", "A product only once it is paid out", "A deposit under the Banks Act"],
 "The FAIS Act lists benefits provided by a pension fund organisation to its members as a financial product, so advice on them is regulated."),
("Under the General Code of Conduct, 'direct marketing' means rendering financial services:",
 "Other than face to face", ["Only by post", "Only to existing clients", "Only from a call centre abroad"],
 "Direct marketing is the rendering of financial services by telephone, internet, post or other electronic media, rather than face to face. Extra disclosure rules apply to it."),
("A product supplier may accept business from an intermediary only if the intermediary:",
 "Is authorised, or acts for an FSP", ["Has been trading for two years", "Belongs to an industry association", "Pays the supplier a security deposit"],
 "The FAIS Act prohibits product suppliers from entering into business with, or accepting business from, a person who is not authorised or is not a representative of an authorised FSP."),
("Which FSP must appoint a compliance officer?",
 "One that has representatives", ["Only one with over 50 staff", "Only a discretionary FSP", "Only an FSP that is owned by a bank"],
 "An authorised FSP with more than one key individual or with one or more representatives must appoint a compliance officer. A sole proprietor with no representatives need not."),
("Who must approve the person appointed as an FSP's compliance officer?",
 "The Authority (FSCA)", ["The FSP's external auditor", "The Ombud for FSPs", "The main product supplier"],
 "A compliance officer must be approved by the Authority, which sets the requirements they must meet."),
("The main role of an FSP's compliance officer is to:",
 "Monitor compliance with the Act", ["Sell products to the biggest clients", "Decide clients' complaints finally", "Set each representative's commission"],
 "The compliance officer monitors compliance with the FAIS Act and the FSP's compliance arrangements. Complaints that the FSP cannot resolve go to the Ombud, not the compliance officer."),
("An FSP's compliance officer must submit reports on the FSP's compliance to:",
 "The Authority", ["The Ombud for FSPs", "The FSP's product suppliers", "Each client of the FSP"],
 "The compliance officer reports to the Authority in the manner and at the times the Authority prescribes."),
("When may the Authority withdraw its approval of a compliance officer?",
 "When no longer fit and proper", ["When the FSP's sales fall", "When a client complains once", "Only after five years"],
 "Section 17(2)(b) of the FAIS Act lets the Authority withdraw approval if the compliance officer has contravened the Act, no longer meets the fit and proper requirements, or no longer complies with the approval criteria."),
("A representative notices that colleagues skip a required disclosure. To whom should this usually be raised first?",
 "The compliance officer", ["The Ombud for FSPs", "The client affected by it", "The product supplier"],
 "The compliance officer monitors the FSP's compliance and is the internal route for a suspected breach. The Ombud deals with clients' complaints, not internal compliance."),
("An FSP that makes investment decisions for clients under a mandate, without asking each time, needs which licence category?",
 "Category II", ["Category I", "Category III", "Category IV"],
 "Under the fit and proper determination (BN 194 of 2017), Category II FSPs are discretionary FSPs, Category III administrative FSPs and Category IV assistance business FSPs. Category I covers FSPs in none of the other categories."),
]
